{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries.md","line":19,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries.tex#def:riemannian-metric","uses":[],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries.tex","label":"def:riemannian-metric","line":20,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Riemannian metric]\n\\label{def:riemannian-metric}\n\n\n\n\nLet $M$ be an $n$-manifold. A \\emph{Riemannian metric} is a smooth\nsection $g\\in\\Gamma(T^*M\\otimes T^*M)$ whose value at each $p\\in M$ is\na positive-definite symmetric bilinear form on $T_pM$. In coordinates\n$(x^1,\\ldots,x^n)$, with $\\partial_i=\\partial/\\partial x^i$,\n\\[\n  g=g_{ij}\\,dx^i\\otimes dx^j,\n  \\qquad g_{ij}=g(\\partial_i,\\partial_j),\n\\]\nand $(g^{ij})=(g_{ij})^{-1}$. The pair $(M,g)$ is a \\emph{Riemannian\nmanifold}.\n\\end{definition}\n\nEvery manifold admits a Riemannian metric by a partition-of-unity\nconstruction. The associated distance is the infimum of lengths of smooth\npaths joining two points. For $r>0$, set\n\\[\n  B_g(p,r)=B(p,r)=\\{q\\in M\\mid d_g(p,q)<r\\}.\n\\]","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Riemannian metric] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7269656d616e6e69616e2d6d6574726963\"></span> <p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> be an <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n$\">$n$</span>-manifold. A <em>Riemannian metric</em> is a smooth section <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g\\in \\Gamma (T^*M\\otimes T^*M)$\">$g\\in \\Gamma (T^*M\\otimes T^*M)$</span> whose value at each <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> is a positive-definite symmetric bilinear form on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_pM$\">$T_pM$</span>. In coordinates <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(x^1,\\ldots ,x^n)$\">$(x^1,\\ldots ,x^n)$</span>, with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\partial _i=\\partial /\\partial x^i$\">$\\partial _i=\\partial /\\partial x^i$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  g=g_{ij}\\, dx^i\\otimes dx^j, \\qquad g_{ij}=g(\\partial _i,\\partial _j),  \\]\">\\[  g=g_{ij}\\, dx^i\\otimes dx^j, \\qquad g_{ij}=g(\\partial _i,\\partial _j),  \\]</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(g^{ij})=(g_{ij})^{-1}$\">$(g^{ij})=(g_{ij})^{-1}$</span>. The pair <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> is a <em>Riemannian manifold</em>.  <p></p>Every manifold admits a Riemannian metric by a partition-of-unity construction. The associated distance is the infimum of lengths of smooth paths joining two points. For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r&gt;0$\">$r&gt;0$</span>, set <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  B_g(p,r)=B(p,r)=\\{ q\\in M\\mid d_g(p,q)&lt;r\\} .  \\]\">\\[  B_g(p,r)=B(p,r)=\\{ q\\in M\\mid d_g(p,q)&lt;r\\} .  \\]</span>","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#sectprelim","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#thm:levi-civita-connection","relations":[],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#thm:levi-civita-connection","title":"thm:levi-civita-connection","label":"thm:levi-civita-connection"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#Koszul","title":"Koszul","label":"Koszul"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:cone","title":"def:cone","label":"def:cone"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:parallel-frame","title":"lem:parallel-frame","label":"lem:parallel-frame"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:local-isometry","title":"def:local-isometry","label":"def:local-isometry"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:submanifold-connection","title":"lem:submanifold-connection","label":"lem:submanifold-connection"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:jacobi-frame-reduction","title":"lem:jacobi-frame-reduction","label":"lem:jacobi-frame-reduction"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:chart-volume-density","title":"def:chart-volume-density","label":"def:chart-volume-density"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#lem:metric-rescaling","title":"lem:metric-rescaling","label":"lem:metric-rescaling"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:local-orthonormal-frame","title":"lem:local-orthonormal-frame","label":"lem:local-orthonormal-frame"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:parallel-gradient-level-sets","title":"lem:parallel-gradient-level-sets","label":"lem:parallel-gradient-level-sets"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#prop:parallel-gradient-splitting","title":"prop:parallel-gradient-splitting","label":"prop:parallel-gradient-splitting"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_BasicsOfRicciFlow#def:ricci-flow","title":"def:ricci-flow","label":"def:ricci-flow"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_ConvergenceResults#def:delta-regular-point","title":"def:delta-regular-point","label":"def:delta-regular-point"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_ConvergenceResults#def:geometric-limit","title":"def:geometric-limit","label":"def:geometric-limit"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support#def:weak-laplacian","title":"def:weak-laplacian","label":"def:weak-laplacian"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support#lem:constant-rescaling-connection-curvature","title":"lem:constant-rescaling-connection-curvature","label":"lem:constant-rescaling-connection-curvature"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support#lem:immersed-patch-induced-connection","title":"lem:immersed-patch-induced-connection","label":"lem:immersed-patch-induced-connection"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","tex":"\\begin{definition}[Riemannian metric]\n\\label{def:riemannian-metric}\n\n\n\n\nLet $M$ be an $n$-manifold. A \\emph{Riemannian metric} is a smooth\nsection $g\\in\\Gamma(T^*M\\otimes T^*M)$ whose value at each $p\\in M$ is\na positive-definite symmetric bilinear form on $T_pM$. In coordinates\n$(x^1,\\ldots,x^n)$, with $\\partial_i=\\partial/\\partial x^i$,\n\\[\n  g=g_{ij}\\,dx^i\\otimes dx^j,\n  \\qquad g_{ij}=g(\\partial_i,\\partial_j),\n\\]\nand $(g^{ij})=(g_{ij})^{-1}$. The pair $(M,g)$ is a \\emph{Riemannian\nmanifold}.\n\\end{definition}\n\nEvery manifold admits a Riemannian metric by a partition-of-unity\nconstruction. The associated distance is the infimum of lengths of smooth\npaths joining two points. For $r>0$, set\n\\[\n  B_g(p,r)=B(p,r)=\\{q\\in M\\mid d_g(p,q)<r\\}.\n\\]","source":"tex/references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries.tex","description":"",